{
  "email": "dana.whitfield@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender requests install of a PDF editor; need department and title for the software request approval (KB-027 step 2)."
}

{
  "query": "approved PDF editor Company Portal software install",
  "reason": "Check whether an approved PDF editor is available in the Company Portal before any other install path."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I can't install that file. It's an unvetted program from an external link, and we don't install software from links received by email. Here's how to get a PDF editor: first, check the Company Portal (Software Center) on your laptop, since approved PDF tools can be installed there yourself. If the tool you need isn't listed, send us the name of the app, the version, why you need it, and your manager's approval, and we'll start a security review. If you'd like, you can also tell us which PDF tasks you need to do, and we can suggest an approved option. Until then, please don't run the setup.exe file from that link.",
  "internal_note": "Ticket from dana.whitfield (user_id 1, CEO, Executive, VIP, active, BL-LT-0101). Request was to install an executable from an external vendor link (free-pdf-tools.example/setup.exe). Per KB-027, we do not install software from an email link and the app needs manager approval plus a security review unless it is in the Company Portal. Nothing was installed and no tools were run on the device. Account is healthy (no lockouts, not blocked). Recommend the user check Company Portal first. Caution: an unsolicited external executable sent by a vendor link to an executive account is a common malware vector. Suggest the technician confirm the vendor and consider a security review before any approval. No escalation made because the request is not yet manager-approved. Note that I could not query the Company Portal catalog directly.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
